Manual smoke checklist (not run in this session — no live Databricks
workspace / running `./scripts/start.sh` instance available):
- [ ] Ask Graph Chat to run an allow-listed Action on an entity → card
      appears under the assistant bubble with action name, entity, and
      description.
- [ ] Click Confirm → buttons disable, status shows "Running…", then
      "Confirmed" once `/dtwin/nodes/action/confirm` resolves, and a new
      assistant message shows the formatted result rows.
- [ ] Click Cancel on a fresh pending card → card is removed immediately
      and no Confirm network call fires.
- [ ] Type "yes" in the chat input instead of clicking Confirm → message
      is sent as ordinary chat text; the action is NOT invoked.
- [ ] Reload the page after a pending card is shown (or wait >120s) →
      clicking the stale Confirm button surfaces the "Action expired"
      error message instead of silently succeeding.

## Let the dev server run without auto-reload (unblocks scenario campaign)

Context: `make scenario-campaign` failed repeatedly at Auto-Map with
"Auto-Map produced no entity SQL within 600s", which wrongly points at the
serving endpoint or warehouse. Root cause was the local dev server: `run.py`
hardcoded `reload=True` over `reload_dirs` covering `src/back` and
`src/agents`, and Auto-Map / the KG build run for minutes in background
threads whose state lives in the in-memory `TaskManager`. Any concurrent
`src/` save restarted uvicorn, killed the thread and orphaned the task
(`GET /tasks/<id>` → 404), so the poll loop burned its full budget. Observed
seven reloads from three parallel workstreams inside one 25-minute window;
OWL generation survived only because it finishes in ~80s.

Changes:

1. `run.py`
   Honour `ONTOBRICKS_NO_RELOAD` (`1/true/yes/on`) to start uvicorn without
   the reloader; only set `reload`/`reload_dirs` when it is unset. Log the
   resolved state as `Uvicorn auto-reload enabled|DISABLED` so the mode is
   verifiable from the log.
2. `scripts/start.sh`
   Add a `--no-reload` flag (exports `ONTOBRICKS_NO_RELOAD=1`) and document
   it in `--help`.
3. `Makefile`
   `scenario-campaign` now warns when the target app is running *with*
   auto-reload, detecting it by topology (a reload-enabled `run.py` forks
   child processes; a no-reload one has none) since the children are plain
   `python3` and reload is enabled in-code, not via `--reload`. Header
   comment documents running the campaign against a no-reload server.

Modified files:
- run.py
- scripts/start.sh
- Makefile
- changelogs/v0.7.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-06.log

