Live verification (campaign against a no-reload server, reload count 0):
- scenario_1 PASSED — Auto-Map completed all 4 chunks (11 entities, 9
  relationships) and the KG build wrote 54,627 triples in 87.6s. Previously
  died in chunk 1/4 on every attempt.
- scenario_2 PASSED.
- scenario_3 FAILED, for two causes unrelated to reload (both pre-existing):
  1. `ONTOBRICKS_SCENARIO_DQ_TIMEOUT` default of 300s is too tight — the run
     was still progressing (89%) when the budget expired. Re-running with
     900s passed in ~190s (122 checks: 99 passed, 22 failed, 1 warning),
     then reasoning inferred 2,381 triples and materialised 2,320.
  2. Graph analysis then 400s: `triplestore_testscenario1_V2_data` does not
     exist. The `_data` snapshot is created by the build pipeline, but
     scenario 3 skips the build when `_graph_built()` (which probes
     `/dtwin/sync/status` on the Lakebase graph) reports data — that is not a
     sufficient proxy for "the UC mapped snapshot exists" on a freshly
     branched version. Left unfixed pending a decision on whether the fix
     belongs in the scenario precondition or in the product.

